-- title:
--   Fraction field of the j-finite chart ring at level Γ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M \ge 1$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Write $F(\Gamma) =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$ attached to pairs of modular forms $f, g$ of some weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$) admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g) \ne 0$. Assume the hypothesis $hj$: the series $q^{-1} \cdot (E_4^3 \eta^{-24})$, i.e. `jqModC ℚ`, lies in $F(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}))$; then `jAt (ΓM M H) hj` denotes the element of $F(\Gamma_H(M))$ whose underlying Laurent series is that series. Let $\Gamma =$ `ΓM M H`, the group attached to $M$ and $H$, and let $R_p \subset \mathbb{Q}$ be the coefficient ring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, i.e. $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. The conclusion is that the subalgebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` of $F(\Gamma)$, consisting of all elements integral over the $R_p$-subalgebra generated by $j$, has $F(\Gamma)$ as its fraction field, the structure map being the inclusion.
--
--   This identifies the function field of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ at level $\Gamma_H(M)$: every modular function for $\Gamma_H(M)$ with rational $q$-expansion is a quotient of two functions integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$. It feeds the stalk computations on that model, namely [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_coeffEmb_mul_stalkRead_eq_stalkRead`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_coeffEmb_mul_stalkRead_eq_stalkRead) and its pointwise variant.
